    {
      "id": "concept-genetic-algorithm-skynet-cost",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "algoritmos genéticos · función de aptitud",
      "questionEn": "Why does the enormous cost assigned to becoming Skynet matter to the joke?",
      "answerEn": "A genetic algorithm searches for good candidate solutions by optimizing a fitness or cost function, so a huge cost can make an unwanted outcome extremely unattractive when the program minimizes cost.",
      "noteEn": "Skynet is the hostile artificial intelligence in the Terminator stories. The code treats an AI takeover as just another outcome to penalize. The title-text warning completes the joke: if the program maximized this cost instead, the enormous number would encourage precisely that outcome.",
      "tags": [
        "concept",
        "genetic algorithm",
        "fitness function",
        "Skynet",
        "optimization",
        "humor"
      ],
      "reviewStatus": "ai-authored-internal-qa",
